{"name":"Jardinière","hex":"#019a74","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jardinière","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An ornamental pot for the display of live or cut flowers; a planter; a plantstand or flowerpot, especially one made of decorated pottery or porcelain.","A vegetable soup or sauce."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jardini%C3%A8re"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jardiniere","blocks":[{"text":"Jardinière is a French word, from the feminine form of \"gardener\". In English it means a decorative flower box or \"planter\", a receptacle or a stand upon which, or into which, plants may be placed, usually indoors. The French themselves mostly refer to tabletop \"planter\" versions of such receptacles as cachepots (\"hide-pots\"). The French tend to use jardinière for larger outdoor containers for plants, and for raised beds in gardens in some sort of isolated frame, such as a stone wall, especially growing vegetables and herbs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Holdcroft_majolica_fish_and_lilies_jardiniere%2C_naturalistic_style_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Holdcroft_majolica_fish_and_lilies_jardiniere%2C_naturalistic_style_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jardiniere","wikidata":"Q4907676"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Ak_%26_cie%2C_jardini%C3%A8re_in_peltro_e_vetro%2C_vienna_1900_ca.jpg/500px-Ak_%26_cie%2C_jardini%C3%A8re_in_peltro_e_vetro%2C_vienna_1900_ca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Ak_%26_cie%2C_jardini%C3%A8re_in_peltro_e_vetro%2C_vienna_1900_ca.jpg/1280px-Ak_%26_cie%2C_jardini%C3%A8re_in_peltro_e_vetro%2C_vienna_1900_ca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi